==Spanish==

[[Image:Large bonfire.jpg|thumb|225px|[[fuego]]]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|es|huego||rare, mostly obsolete}}
* {{alter|es|fogo||rare, obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|es|osp|fuego}}, from {{inh|es|LL.|focus||fire}}, from {{inh|es|la|focus||hearth}}. The form {{m|es|huego}}, which began to be used around 1500, was mostly replaced by the form starting with -f-<ref>{{R:DCECH}}</ref>. Compare {{cog|pt|fogo}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|fuel}}. Compare also {{cog|en|focus}}. {{doublet|es|foco}}, which is a borrowing from Latin.

===Pronunciation===
{{es-IPA}}
* {{a|non-standard}} {{IPA|es|[ˈɸweɣo]|[ˈhweɣo]}}
* {{hyph|es|fue|go}}
* {{audio|es|LL-Q1321 (spa)-Rodelar-fuego.wav|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{es-noun|m}}

# [[fire]]

